{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-71835" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $|\\,p\\,|=8$, $|\\,q\\,|=4$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ Find the vector projection of $p$ onto $q$ in terms of the vector $q.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-71835" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p & =|\\,p\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $q:$\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{q}{|\\,q\\,|}=\\frac{q}{4}=\\frac{1}{4}q\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,p & ={\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p\\cdot u \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}q \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}q\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-71835" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7459781824c6f21b40d26082ff3711104219233040a184de8850470e27f22fdf"} {"question" "q-71835" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-71835" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\sqrt{2}q"] ["math" "2q"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}q"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}q"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}q"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-71835" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{2}q"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-19220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $|\\,a\\,|=36$, $|\\,b\\,|=6$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta ={135}^{∘}.$ Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b$ in terms of the vector $b.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-19220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =|\\,a\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =36\\operatorname{cos}⁡({135}^{∘}) \\\\  & =36\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-18\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $b:$\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{b}{|\\,b\\,|}=\\frac{b}{6}=\\frac{1}{6}b\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & ={\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a\\cdot u \\\\  & =(-18\\sqrt{2})\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}b \\\\  & =-3\\sqrt{2}b\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-19220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7459781824c6f21b40d26082ff3711104219233040a184de8850470e27f22fdf"} {"question" "q-19220" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-19220" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-12\\sqrt{2}b"] ["math" "-18\\sqrt{2}b"] ["math" "-3\\sqrt{2}b"] ["math" "-6\\sqrt{2}b"] ["math" "-9\\sqrt{2}b"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-19220" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3\\sqrt{2}b"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-316441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $|\\,a\\,|=4$, $|\\,b\\,|=8\\sqrt{2}$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ Find the vector projection of $b$ onto $a$ in terms of the vector $a.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,b=$\n{{field-1}}\n$a$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-316441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{a}\\,b & =|\\,b\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $a:$\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{a}{|\\,a\\,|}=\\frac{a}{4}=\\frac{1}{4}a\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,b & ={\\text{comp}}_{a}\\,b\\cdot u \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}a \\\\  & =2\\,a\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-316441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7459781824c6f21b40d26082ff3711104219233040a184de8850470e27f22fdf"} {"question" "q-316441" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-316441" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-275228" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $|\\,p\\,|=6$, $|\\,q\\,|=12$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta ={150}^{∘}.$ Find the vector projection of $q$ onto $p$ in terms of the vector $p.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{p}\\,q=$\n{{field-1}}\n$p$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-275228" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{p}\\,q & =|\\,q\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =12\\operatorname{cos}⁡({150}^{∘}) \\\\  & =12\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =-6\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $p:$\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{p}{|\\,p\\,|}=\\frac{p}{6}=\\frac{1}{6}p\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{p}\\,q & ={\\text{comp}}_{p}\\,q\\cdot u \\\\  & =-6\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}p \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{3}\\,p\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-275228" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7459781824c6f21b40d26082ff3711104219233040a184de8850470e27f22fdf"} {"question" "q-275228" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-275228" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\sqrt{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-71838" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $|\\,c\\,|=10$, $|\\,d\\,|=2\\sqrt{3}$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta ={30}^{∘}.$ Find the vector projection of $c$ onto $d$ in terms of the vector $d.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-71838" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{d}\\,c & =|\\,c\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =10\\operatorname{cos}⁡({30}^{∘}) \\\\  & =10\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $d:$\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{d}{|\\,d\\,|}=\\frac{d}{2\\sqrt{3}}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}}d\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c & ={\\text{comp}}_{d}\\,c\\cdot u \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}d\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-71838" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7459781824c6f21b40d26082ff3711104219233040a184de8850470e27f22fdf"} {"question" "q-71838" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-71838" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "5d"] ["math" "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{5}d"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{5}d"] ["math" "\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{3}d"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}d"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-71838" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{2}d"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-18377" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨0,-3,1⟩$ and $b=⟨\\sqrt{2},1,0⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-18377" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{0\\cdot \\sqrt{2}+(-3)\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 0}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{3}⟨\\sqrt{2},1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\sqrt{2},-1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "f