or the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,u & =\\frac{u\\cdot v}{v\\cdot v}v \\\\  & =\\frac{{u}_{x}{v}_{x}+{u}_{y}{v}_{y}+{u}_{z}{v}_{z}}{{v}_{x}^{2}+{v}_{y}^{2}+{v}_{z}^{2}}v \\\\  & =\\frac{(1)\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot 1+(1)\\cdot 0}{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}}v \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{5}v \\\\  & =⟨\\,0,0,0\\,⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-317924" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7459781824c6f21b40d26082ff3711104219233040a184de8850470e27f22fdf"} {"question" "q-317924" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-317924" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-317924" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-317924" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-317924" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-317924" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-316761" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $r=⟨-5,1,3⟩$ and $s=⟨n,-2,4⟩.$ Given that the projection of $r$ onto $s$ is the zero vector, find the value of $n.$\n\n$n=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-316761" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $r$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $s$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\nr⊥s\\,⟹\\,r\\cdot s=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot s & ={r}_{x}\\cdot {s}_{x}+{r}_{y}\\cdot {s}_{y}+{r}_{z}\\cdot {s}_{z} \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot n+1\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-5n-2+12 \\\\  & =10-5n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot s & =0 \\\\ 10-5n & =0 \\\\ n & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-316761" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7459781824c6f21b40d26082ff3711104219233040a184de8850470e27f22fdf"} {"question" "q-316761" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-316761" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-275237" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Given that the projection of $a$ onto $b$ is the zero vector, find the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-275237" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na⊥b\\,⟹\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =-2\\cdot x+1\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2x+5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ -2x+5 & =0 \\\\ 2x & =5 \\\\ x & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-275237" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7459781824c6f21b40d26082ff3711104219233040a184de8850470e27f22fdf"} {"question" "q-275237" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-275237" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-212458" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨-5,-3,1⟩$ and $b=⟨x,-2,-3⟩.$ Given that the projection of $a$ onto $b$ is the zero vector, find the value of $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-212458" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na⊥b\\,⟹\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =-5\\cdot x+(-3)\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =3-5x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ 3-5x & =0 \\\\ -5x & =-3 \\\\ x & =\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-212458" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7459781824c6f21b40d26082ff3711104219233040a184de8850470e27f22fdf"} {"question" "q-212458" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-212458" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{5}"] ["math" "-\\frac{2}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "q-212458" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "d0735f36e4489cf129b060df9782f01d73b0c72b260928e8aab3f7e9ff655550"} {"question" "e-14617" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $|\\,\\mathbf{a}\\,|=8,|\\,\\mathbf{b}\\,|=4$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta = \\dfrac{5\\pi}{6}.$ Find the vector projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$ in terms of the vector $\\mathbf{b}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/example-14617.json" "file_sha256" "c3a63a80d8ab0c39b4c570d4a22b16632363e70b7b40672ceaec9fe25d81d337"} {"question" "e-14617" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =|\\,a\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =8\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =-4\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf{b}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u} = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{b}}{|\\,\\mathbf{b}\\,|} = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{b}}{4} = \\dfrac{1}{4} \\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & ={\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a\\cdot u \\\\  & =-4\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}b \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{3}b\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/example-14617.json" "file_sha256" "c3a63a80d8ab0c39b4c570d4a22b16632363e70b7b40672ceaec9fe25d81d337"} {"question" "e-14618" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 1,-3,5 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 5,-4,0 \\rangle$. Find the vector projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/example-14618.json" "file_sha256" "7f6b5ddcdf9d1ec55dce58c09b66fdd24e34b716af18e02ebf61f4ec219ffe24"} {"question" "e-14618" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 5+(-3)\\cdot (-4)+5\\cdot 0}{{5}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{0}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{41}⟨5,-4,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{85}{41},-\\frac{68}{41},0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/example-14618.json" "file_sha256" "7f6b5ddcdf9d1ec55dce58c09b66fdd24e34b716af18e02ebf61f4ec219ffe24"} {"question" "e-14619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$. Find the vector projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/example-14619.json" "file_sha256" "fa1135cc133105c7e5c1749a8d5dacd867180d7702004b284fd60ace6f3f8eb1"} {"question" "e-14619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 5+1\\cdot (-1)}{{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}b \\\\  & =⟨0,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/example-14619.json" "file_sha256" "fa1135cc133105c7e5c1749a8d5dacd867180d7702004b284fd60ace6f3f8eb1"}] "usage" {"e-14618" [] "e-14619" [] "e-14617" []} "basis" 814 "retractions" [[17592186105401 :question/problem "Suppose that $\\mid \\,\\mathbf{a}\\,|=8, \\mid \\,\\mathbf{b}\\,|=4$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta = \\dfrac{5\\pi}{6}$. Find the vector projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$ in terms of the vector $\\mathbf{b}$."] [17592186105401 :question/worked-solution "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ncomp_{b}a &= \\mid a \\mid \\cos θ \\\\\n&= 8\\cos (\\frac{5π}{6}) \\\\\n&= 8 \\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\\n&=-4\\sqrt{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf{b}$:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u} = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{b}}{\\mid \\,\\mathbf{b}\\, \\mid} = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{b}}{4} = \\dfrac{1}{4} \\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nproj_{b}a &= comp_{b}a \\cdot u \\\\\n&=-4\\sqrt{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{4}b \\\\\n&=-\\sqrt{3}b\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186105402 :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nproj_{b}a &= \\frac{a \\cdot b}{b \\cdot b}b \\\\\n&= \\frac{a_{x}b_{x} + a_{y}b_{y} + a_{z}b_{z}}{b_{x}^{2} + b_{y}^{2} + b_{z}^{2}}b \\\\\n&= (1 \\cdot 5 + (-3) \\cdot (-4) + 5 \\cdot 0)/(5^{2} + (-4)^{2} + 0^{2})b \\\\\n&= \\frac{17}{41}⟨5,-4, 0⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{85}{41},-\\frac{68}{41}, 0⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186105403 :question/problem "Let $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$. Find the vector projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$."] [17592186105403 :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nproj_{b}a &= \\frac{a \\cdot b}{b \\cdot b}b \\\\\n&= \\frac{a_{x}b_{x} + a_{y}b_{y} + a_{z}b_{z}}{b_{x}^{2} + b_{y}^{2} + b_{z}^{2}}b \\\\\n&= (1 \\cdot 1 + 0 \\cdot 5 + 1 \\cdot (-1))/(1^{2} + 5^{2} + (-1)^{2})b \\\\\n&= (0)/(1^{2} + 5^{2} + (-1)^{2})b \\\\\n&= ⟨0, 0, 0⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
